QuestGuidance.Register("en",461,{
[14721]="7000EF78\n1\tDefeat ice-worms (total: 20)\tIce-worms can be found throughout Talvi-mûri. Jyrki has asked you to defeat the furry worms that threaten the Lossoth encampments.\n2\tTalk to Jyrki\tJyrki is at the hunter's way-post at the northern end of Talvi-mûri. You should return to Jyrki with news of your success.\n",
[14722]="7002D528\n1\tFind a blacksmith in Bree-town to help you\tA blacksmith in Bree-town should be able to help us make a new set of horseshoes.\n2\tFind an old horseshoe\030Obtain crates of nails (total: 2)\030Obtain scrap metal (total: 3)\tThe items needed by the blacksmith to forge new horseshoes can be found around the forge area.\n3\tBring the items to Matt Haywood in Bree-town\tMatt Haywood can be found at his forge near the Western gate of Bree-town, and is ready to help make the horseshoes.\n4\tBring the horseshoes to the stable-helper in Combe\tThe stable-helper in Combe will be happy to receive the horseshoes for the newly arrived horse.\n",
[14723]="7002D5B8\n1\tFind a blacksmith to help fill the horseshoe order\tThe blacksmiths of Bree-town can be found near the West-gate.\n2\tFind an old horseshoe\030Obtain crates of horseshoe nails (total: 2)\030Obtain scrap-metal (total: 3)\tAll of the items required by the blacksmith should be found here in Bree-town. The old horseshoe should be in the fields across the street. The scrap-metal can usually be found among the trash in Beggar's Alley, and the crates of nails should be in the Market Square.\n3\tBring the items to Flint Oakhewer in Bree-town\tFlint is near the Bree-town's West-gate, always busy shaping iron at his forge. Flint is prepared to make the horseshoes once you can bring the supplies he required back to him.\n4\tReturn to Éogar with the horseshoes\tÉogar can be found at his farm in the Horsefields of Bree.\n",
[14724]="70016B3D\n1\tThe Orc Watch is the main Iron Garrison settlement in the Redhorn Lodes, located on the western side of that area. There are many dwarves at the Orc-watch. Perhaps one of them knows why the recently deceased Nykr valued this little hand-made locket so highly.\t\n",
[14725]="70032C2D\n1\tCollect Knakk's tools from his nearby crate\tKnakk is camped close to the Grand Stair and is trying to figure out the puzzle of a locket which Kafli was holding when he died. He thinks the puzzle is finally solved, with a little help from a tool out of his nearby crate. He is eager to finally see what is inside and perhaps find an answer for why Kafli was so afraid to lose it.\n2\tReturn to Knakk to help him open the locket\tKnakk is camped close to the Grand Stair and is trying to figure out the puzzle of a locket which Kafli was holding when he died. He seems to be very close to finally figuring out the locket's intriguing puzzle. You should bring Knakk's tools to him.\n",
[14726]="7004785F\n1\tTorngroth can be found far to the north in North Ithilien, Cair Andros can be found to the south-west of Henneth Annûn, Osgiliath can be found to the east of Minas Tirith, and Ioreth can be found in the High Hall within the Masters' Tier of Minas Tirith. Mílgamel has asked you to investigate Cair Andros, Osgiliath, and Torngroth in the hope of finding more pages from \"Worts and Weeds.\" She also has asked you to return to Ioreth to obtain Galathir's transcription of the book.\t\n2\tFind Mílgamel at the Camp of the Host\tMílgamel can be found at the Camp of the Host in the far north of North Ithilien. You have found many pages of \"Worts and Weeds\" and now surely have a completed volume between them. You should seek out Mílgamel at the Camp of the Host and deliver them to her.\n3\tTalk to Mílgamel at the Camp of the Host\tMílgamel can be found at the Camp of the Host in the far north of North Ithilien. You have arrived at the Camp of the Host and should now speak to Mílgamel.\n4\tBind the pages into Mílgamel's transcription of \"Worts and Weeds\"\tMílgamel's transcription of \"Worts and Weeds\" can be found beside her at the Camp of the Host. Mílgamel has asked you to bind the new pages into her transcription of \"Worts and Weeds.\"\n5\tTalk to Mílgamel\tMílgamel can be found at the Camp of the Host in the far north of North Ithilien. You have finished binding the completed volume of \"Worts and Weeds\" and should now speak to Mílgamel.\n",
[14727]="700456A2\n1\tSpeak with Êkh-buri-Dhûr\030Speak with Gnô-maka-Ghûr\tÊkh-buri-Dhûr and Gnô-maka-Ghûr are in Drû Bhûta. You should speak with Êkh-buri-Dhûr and Gnô-maka-Ghûr before the wedding ceremony begins.\n2\tPick up smooth river pebbles (total: 5)\tThe sacred wedding pebbles can be found in Drû Bhûta. Êkh-buri-Dhûr asks you to hold the sacred wedding pebbles.\n3\tCatch a fish worthy of this union\tFish can be caught from the Drúnen River in Drû Bhûta. Êkh-buri-Dhûr asks you to catch the sacred wedding fish.\n4\tTickle the goat\tThe wedding goat can be found in Drû Bhûta. Êkh-buri-Dhûr asks you to tickle the sacred wedding goat.\n5\tCongratulate Êkh-buri-Dhûr\030Congratulate Gnô-maka-Ghûr\tÊkh-buri-Dhûr and Gnô-maka-Ghûr are in Drû Bhûta. You should speak with the newly wed couple.\n6\tCongratulate Ôk-weni-Dhûr\tÔk-weni-Dhûr is in Drû Bhûta. You should speak with Ôk-weni-Dhûr.\n",
[14728]="70008662\n1\tMine gem-bearing rocks (total: 3)\tGem-bearing rocks of the sort Bothwar described can be found outside the entrance to Maethad. He told you to follow the road north from Gabilshathûr until you could turn east and pass through the sparse trees of Gorothlad. Bothwar is annoyed that he was pulled from his mining efforts to undertake guard-duty and has asked you to finish his mining.\n2\tBring gemstone-rocks to Bothwar\tBothwar is on the bridge in the middle of Gabilshathûr, west and south of Gorothlad. You have mined the gem-bearing rocks of which Bothwar spoke and should return to him with the fruits of your labour.\n",
[14729]="70040000\n1\tHeal injured soldiers (total: 4)\tThe injured must be tended to before their wounds become too great.\n",
[14730]="700430D2\n1\tCollect kingsfoil outside Tumladen (total: 8)\030Collect a loaf of bread\tKingsfoil can be found along the roads and on the fields outside Tumladen. A loaf of bread can be found within Tumladen. Faltharan has asked for your aid in obtaining food and healing herbs for his father.\n2\tDeliver the kingsfoil and bread to Faltharan\tFaltharan and Lord Sirgon can be found in Tumladen in northern Upper Lebennin. You have gathered a loaf of bread and a great deal of kingsfoil and should now return to Faltharan.\n",
[14731]="70045438\n1\tThe Black Serpent can be found in the Blood of the Black Serpent instance.\t\n2\tLet events transpire\tStay near Théoden.\n3\tSpeak with Théoden\tThéoden can be found in the Blood of the Black Serpent instance.\n4\tSpeak with Bregdal\tBregdal can be found on the Field of Onslaught. You should speak with Bregdal.\n",
[14732]="7004543D\n1\tDefeat foes on the Field of Onslaught (total: 10)\tThe Enemy can be found on the Field of Onslaught, upon the fields of Pelennor. Defeat foes on the Field of Onslaught.\n2\tSpeak with Bregdal\tBregdal can be found on the Field of Onslaught. You should speak with Bregdal.\n3\tSpeak with Bregdal when next you meet\tBregdal can be found at Kings' End. You should speak with Bregdal.\n",
[14733]="7004543C\n1\tDefeat the Gloom of Nurn\tThe Gloom of Nurn can be found in the Silent Street instance.\n2\tLet events transpire\tStay near Gandalf.\n3\tSpeak with Gandalf\030Speak with Peregrin Took\tGandalf and Peregrin Took can be found in the Silent Street instance.\n4\tSpeak with Bregdal at Kings' End\tBregdal can be found at Kings' End. You should speak with Bregdal.\n",
[14734]="7004543A\n1\tDefeat foes at Kings' End (total: 10)\tThe Enemy can be found at Kings' End, upon the fields of Pelennor. Defeat foes at Kings' End.\n2\tSpeak with Bregdal\tBregdal can be found at Kings' End. You should speak with Bregdal.\n3\tSpeak with Bregdal when next you meet\tBregdal can be found at Riders' Stand. You should speak with Bregdal.\n",
[14735]="70045439\n1\tDefeat the Forsaken Reaver\tThe Forsaken Reaver can be found in the Quays of the Harlond instance.\n2\tMeet Aragorn on the hill across the river\tMeet Aragorn on the hill across the river.\n3\tLet events transpire\tStay near Aragorn.\n4\tSpeak with Duinhir\030Speak with Aragorn\030Speak with Éomer\tDuinhir, Aragorn, and Éomer can be found in the Quays of the Harlond instance.\n5\tSpeak with Bregdal at Riders' Stand\tBregdal can be found at Riders' Stand. You should speak with Bregdal.\n6\tSpeak with Bregdal at the Ruin of Pel Dúven\tBregdal can be found at the Ruin of Pel Dúven. You should speak with Bregdal.\n",
[14736]="70045437\n1\tSpeak with Bregdal at the Threshold of the City\tBregdal can be found at the Threshold of the City. You should speak with Bregdal.\n",
[14737]="700358B2\n1\tDefeat Daegul in Fiskworth\tDefeat as many Daegul as you can while making your way through Fiskworth.\n2\tDefeat Daegul in Fiskworth (total: 6)\tDefeat as many Daegul as you can while making your way through Fiskworth.\n3\tCompleted\tClearing the area of Daegul should make traversing through Fiskworth much easier now.\n",
[14738]="7002F97A\n1\tTalk to Reeve Athelward\tReeve Athelward resides in his Mead Hall, at the eastern edge of Cliving. Athelward has asked you to accompany him onto the battlefield, so that he may set an example for his men and to witness your prowess.\n2\tTalk to Reeve Athelward\tReeve Athelward resides in his Mead Hall, at the eastern edge of Cliving. Athelward would like to speak with you following your battle in the Norcrofts.\n",
[14739]="70018C1A\n1\tGather branches from the bushes (total: 5)\tThe bushes can be found to the west of Duillond. Anglalaith has asked you to gather some branches from several bushes so that he may finish making his Yule wreaths.\n2\tBring the branches to Anglalaith\030Collect Fir Branch (total: 5)\tAnglalaith is at Duillond. Anglalaith will be pleased to receive the branches you gathered and begin work on more wreaths.\n",
[14740]="7004A8F0\n1\tClear webs from the road leading to Cirith Ungol (total: 8)\tWebs can be found along the road to Cirith Ungol in western Lhingris. Práguk has asked you to clear webs from the road leading to Cirith Ungol.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have cleared the road to Cirith Ungol of webs.\n",
[14741]="70016B94\n1\tDefeat Lûrkh\tLûrkh is at Drû-garmadh to the south-east of Mekhem-bizru. Dagfari does not believe the siege-weapons will stop until their mastermind, Lûrkh, has been defeated.\n2\tTalk to Dagfari at Mekhem-bizru\tDagfari is at Mekhem-bizru, north-west of Drû-garmadh. Dagfari will want to hear of the defeat of Lûrkh and the end of the siege-camp.\n",
[14742]="70035801\n1\tDefeat enemies in the Writhendowns (total: 10)\tThe forces of Isengard can be found in the Writhendowns. You should ride to the Writhendowns and defeat the enemies of Wildermore.\n2\tReturn to Ealswith\tEalswith is in Forlaw. You should return to Ealswith.\n",
[14743]="70035A73\n1\tDefeat Easterlings in the Writhendowns (total: 10)\tThe Easterlings in the Writhendowns can be reached by speaking with Dudoc in Forlaw. You should travel to the tundra of the Writhendowns and defeat Easterlings there.\n2\tReturn to Dudoc in Forlaw\tDudoc is in Forlaw. You should return to Dudoc.\n",
[14744]="7003585F\n1\tLight Watch-fires (total: 3)\tWatch-fires can be found along the higher cliffs nearest the lake's edge in the south-western Writhendowns. You should light Watch-fires to let the watchmen of Forlaw know that the Writhendowns has not entirely fallen under enemy sway.\n2\tReturn to Ealswith\tEalswith is in Forlaw. You should return to Ealswith.\n",
[14745]="70059907\n1\tDestroy spider cocoons at Writhenset (total: 10)\tSpider cocoons can be found at Writhenset in the Wildwood. You should destroy spider cocoons at Writhenset.\n",
[14746]="70059788\n1\tDestroy supply crates at Writhenset (total: 10)\tSupply crates can be found at Writhenset in the Wildwood. You should destroy supply crates at Writhenset.\n",
[14747]="70059785\n1\tDefeat foes at Writhenset\tFoes can be found at Writhenset in the Wildwood. You should defeat foes at Writhenset.\n2\tDefeat foes at Writhenset (total: 12)\tFoes can be found at Writhenset in the Wildwood. You should defeat foes at Writhenset.\n",
[14748]="7005B1F0\n1\tFind Orkish notes (total: 5)\tOrkish notes with useful information may be scattered around Dalugronk.\n2\tTalk to Féli in Aslíf\tYou have found a number of Orkish notes, each with varying degrees of usefulness to the Gabil'akkâ. Féli in Aslíf will be interested to hear of your findings. Aslíf is on the upper tier of Deepscrave.\n",
[14749]="70025B77\n1\tCollect Writs of Honour (total: 10)\tOst Heryn is south of Torogethir's camp. Torogethir asked you to venture within Ost Heryn and collect several Writs of Honour from the spirits within.\n2\tBring the Writs of Honour to Torogethir at his camp in Parth Aduial\tTorogethir is at his camp, north of Ost Heryn. Torogethir will be eager to examine the Writs and see if there is a way he can honour them.\n",
[14750]="7002ED7B\n1\tDefeat the Wyrm-father\t\n2\tDefeat the Wyrm-father\tThe Wyrm-father perches upon Fang Tor, outside the Wyrmdelf. You should defeat the great drake known as the Wyrm-father.\n3\tBring the Wyrm-father's scale to the Rohirrim at Eaworth\tThere are Rohirrim at Eaworth, south-west of the Wyrmdelf. You should return to Eaworth and tell someone of the Wyrm-father's defeat.\n",
[14751]="70030F8D\n1\tDefeat the Wyrm-father\t\n2\tDefeat the Wyrm-father\tThe Wyrm-father perches upon Fang Tor, outside the Wyrmdelf. You should defeat the great drake known as the Wyrm-father.\n3\tBring the Wyrm-father's scale to the Rohirrim at Eaworth\tThere are Rohirrim at Eaworth, south-west of the Wyrmdelf. You should return to Eaworth and tell someone of the Wyrm-father's defeat.\n",
[14752]="70035593\n1\tPick yarrow for a poultice (total: 6)\030Collect snow for a poultice (total: 4)\tYarrow and snow can be found to the east of the refugees' cave in the northern High Knolls. You should collect yarrow and snow for a poultice to try to save the Thane.\n2\tBring the poultice ingredients to Céolflad\tCéolflad can be found in the refugees' cave north of Byre Tor in the High Knolls. You should return to Céolflad with the yarrow and snow.\n",
})
